**Picks a minister for cabinet posts out of the country's pool.** 0x4F06D0 to the `ret 0xC` at 0x4F08E1, read whole on the listing (FINDINGS-government.md A.5). For each post index i from 1 to the end of `ministers (+0x618)` (index 0, the null post, is skipped), the post being `GetGovernmentPositions()->[i]`:

- skip unless `refillAll`, or the post's holder is the null minister (CMinister slot 8 is ReturnTrue, CNullMinister's ReturnFalse - 'is a real minister', no dates);
- with `electedOnly`, skip unless the post's bit (its +0x4C) is set in `government (+0xDFC)->elected_positions (+0x68)`;
- walk `PossibleMinisters (+0x160)` in list order: a minister **of the ruling ideology** (+0x1140) who lists the post among his postings (+0x5C) is taken at once and the walk stops; otherwise a minister **of the ruling ideology's group** (ideology +0x50) who lists it becomes the candidate - **replacing any earlier candidate, so the last such in the pool wins**; otherwise one who lists it becomes the candidate only while there is none - **the first such wins**;
- a candidate found is written to `ministers[post->index]`; none leaves the post as it was, `refillAll` or not.

Not asked: his dates, whether he already holds another post (one man can fill several), whether the post is changeable, his loyalty. Both ideology tests dereference the ruling ideology with no null test, so a country with no ruling party and a non-empty pool faults (at 0x4F083B). **Reproduces the start save**: replaying it on the saved pool and ruling ideology gives all 220 posts of the 22 countries whose history names no minister (CRO, DDR, ICL, VIC and the rest), the 'last of the group' rule included (Iceland's head of government is 581006, the last of three liberals who list the post).

Callers (args `refillAll, electedOnly`): SetUpCountryForNewGame 0x4D7538 (0, 0) - a new game, empty posts only; CCountry_HoldElection 0x4FC3C3 (1, 1); CCoupEffect::Execute 0x9A1721 (1, 0); CGovernmentEffect::Execute 0x9A10F7 (1, 0); MakeVassal 0x4DA3E4 (1, 0); CCreateVassalCommand::Execute 0x54C2EE (1, 0); CLiberateCountryCommand::Execute 0x54CED4 (1, 0); ReleaseProvinces 0x4C21D9 (1, 0); CReleaseVassalEffect::Execute 0x9AF145 (1, 0). Nothing calls it when a minister dies, when a law changes, daily or on a load.
